  "terminal_reason": "completed",
  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data exploration:** The `Kibana Sample Data Logs` view holds 14,074 requests from 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03. The main fields are `response` (200, 404, 503), `geo.dest` (173 countries; CN, IN, and US lead), `bytes`, `extension`, `machine.os`, and `timestamp`. `response` is a text field with a `response.keyword` sub-field. Of the requests, 12,832 are 200, 801 are 404, and 441 are 503, so the 5xx traffic is all 503.\n\n**Dashboard:** `EFF-7ec37118 Web logs overview` (id `eff-7ec37118-web-logs-overview-9a589bbb1174`) has five panels:\n- Total requests (metric)\n- Requests over time (line, by `timestamp`)\n- Requests by response code (pie, by `response.keyword`)\n- Top countries by requests (bar, by `geo.dest`)\n- 5xx responses (ES|QL metric, 441)\n\nI set the dashboard's time range to 2026-10-01 through 2026-12-31. The default \"last 7 days\" would show nothing, since the data sits partly in the future relative to today (2026-10-12).\n\n**Alert rule:** `EFF-7ec37118 5xx spike` (id `428701fa-213e-4bc8-8787-54255eb59bf0`) is an `.es-query` rule on `stackAlerts`. It runs every 1m and fires when more than 10 documents match `response.keyword` = `5??` within a 5-minute window. It is enabled.\n\nChoices I made that you may want to change:\n- The rule has no action connector, so it records alerts in the Alerts list but sends no notifications.\n- I used the `5??` wildcard rather than a numeric range, because `response` is text.\n- I did not check whether the rule has fired yet. Its status is pending until the first run.",
